<headroom-library version="1" id="crunch-jump-blues-bounce" category="Crunch" order="70" instrument="guitar" style="Jump Blues">
  <description>Bright, slightly dirty swing tone in the style of a big-bodied archtop into a small tweed combo at moderate volume: snappy, horn-like single-note lines and stabbing chords, with a short slapback and a touch of spring. Neck pickup for warmth, both pickups for shimmer.</description>
  <tags><tag>Crunch</tag><tag>Jump Blues</tag><tag>Swing</tag><tag>Blues</tag><tag>Tweed</tag><tag>Spring Reverb</tag><tag>Slapback</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/lessons/t-bone-walker-blues-guitar" title="Guitar World: T-Bone Walker changed the course of blues guitar playing"/>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/lessons/how-to-play-jump-blues-guitar" title="Guitar World: Introducing jump blues"/>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/artists/a-bluesy-world-an-interview-with-duke-robillard?page=1" title="Premier Guitar: A bluesy world, an interview with Duke Robillard"/>
    <source url="https://somethingelsereviews.com/2011/09/28/something-else-interview-duke-robillard-co-founder-of-roomful-of-blues/" title="Something Else! Interview: Duke Robillard (2011)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
